  "assessment": "Reconciled twelve direct interests, four stable directions, thirty-three curricular topics, seven illustrations and eleven individual outcomes. Nine generator rows belong to the broad core; cognitive/data owns two, molecular/health four and evolutionary psychobiology one. The two additional priorities are supported by official optional packages. Evolution remains evidenced but unattempted after the maximum; no omnibus residual cluster or inherited split-target evidence is used.",
  "sourceSupport": {
    "19861–19876": "Current programme, introductory course and mandatory biological/cognitive courses corroborate the target, while the choice page lists cognitive/molecular/evolutionary study packages. These are not formal selected routes.",
    "19877–19909": "Named genetics, cell/neural biology, cognition, evolution, regulation, methods, EEG, programming, bioethics and project entries corroborate the support-only topics. The introductory course expressly discusses ADHD, neurotransmitter systems and disorders; individual neurochemical examples do not define whole UCR courses.",
    "19910–19916": "Illustrations remain search-only. Free-will debates, neural disorders and EEG/molecular experiments are examples, not additional obligatory components or separate UCR generators.",
    "19917–19927": "Postgraduate and employment outcomes remain individual or conditional search terms, not admissions, clinical-treatment or professional-qualification entitlements. The current programme explicitly distinguishes psychobiological research from psychology/medicine preparation for treating patients. No such entitlement appears in the finished comparison."
  },
